WEBVTT

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.122
When the Lord Jesus spoke of the mystery
of God's kingdom, He used the parable of

00:00:04.122 --> 00:00:04.610
the sower.

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:14.497
He Himself is God's word, like a seed sown
into the human heart to grow and bear

00:00:14.497 --> 00:00:15.210
fruit.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.200
First, God's kingdom is Christ growing
within us.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:28.140
It becomes a realm of life: the church
life we live today.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:37.488
We encourage everyone who has been
baptized and saved to continue steadfastly
in the

00:00:37.488 --> 00:00:38.720
church life.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.720
It is within this realm of life that your
life can grow.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:51.640
Fish need to live in water. Out of water,
they cannot survive for long.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.140
Birds need the air; they cannot live
underwater.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:06.415
Likewise, Christians need a suitable
environment for life to grow: an ecology
that

00:01:06.415 --> 00:01:08.420
supports growth.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.960
Second, God's kingdom is the realm in
which Christ rules.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.560
As we grow in life, we learn to submit to
the Lord.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:24.285
For Christ to rule, we must step down from
the throne where we make every decision

00:01:24.285 --> 00:01:24.920
ourselves.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:32.760
We let Christ not only make His home in
our hearts, but also be our Lord and King.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:37.020
We must learn to follow and obey Him.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:44.510
We have believed and been regenerated. As
His life grows, He reigns within us.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:47.670
Christ wants to make His home in our
hearts.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:54.170
When the Lord returns, all things will be
headed up in Christ.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:02:00.170
So today, we first let Christ be our Head.
